      "message": "The VirtIO socket device assigns an array of virtqueue on heap, each item having 512 bytes, with 64KiB, we hit an error when initializing the driver [1]:\n```\n07-06 11:44:14.784 shell 15546 15573 I rialto  : rialto_test: [DEBUG]   VirtIO Socket\n07-06 11:44:14.785 shell 15546 15573 I rialto  : rialto_test: [DEBUG] Device features: Feature(RING_EVENT_IDX | VERSION_1 | ACCESS_PLATFORM)\n07-06 11:44:14.785 shell 15546 15573 I rialto  : rialto_test: [DEBUG] config: 0x2022000\n07-06 11:44:14.786 shell 15546 15573 I rialto  : rialto_test: [DEBUG] guest cid: 2169\n07-06 11:44:14.788 shell 15546 15573 I rialto  : rialto_test: panicked at \u0027memory allocation of 512 bytes failed\u0027, prebuilts/rust/linux-x86/1.70.0/src/stdlibs/library/alloc/src/alloc.rs:409:13\n```\n[1] https://cs.android.com/android/platform/superproject/+/master:external/rust/crates/virtio-drivers/src/device/socket/vsock.rs;l\u003d267;drc\u003d91b9730f88c54183aae71e4b79d093ed1914c9a2\n\nAbout SIZE_128KB, it is consistent with pvmfw\u0027s heap configuration [2].\n[2] https://cs.android.com/android/platform/superproject/+/master:packages/modules/Virtualization/pvmfw/src/entry.rs;l\u003d64;drc\u003d6a4808c03a31e6546ea5f68a976b1dd68f5b9f93",
